    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d884">

                <pb facs="0954" n="1788" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1788"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111N83/39</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Christiania</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-03T19:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 3, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 4, 12.30
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1209. My telegram No. 1189, September 29, 5 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d884-f1"/>
                    I am in receipt of a <hi rendition="#italic">note verbale</hi> from the Foreign
                    Office dated today reading as follows in translation from the French: <pb
                        facs="0955" n="1789" xml:id="pg1789"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The Ministry for Foreign Affairs has the honor to bring to the knowledge
                            of the Legation of the United States of America that automatic [contact]
                            mines will be placed by the Royal Norwegian Navy in the part of
                            Norwegian territorial waters comprised between 59° 8′ and 59° 25′ north
                            latitude and [west] of 5° 10′ longitude east of Greenwich. For this
                            reason the above indicated areas will be closed to ordinary traffic from
                            Monday, October 7, 1918.</p>
                        <p>The Legation of Norway at Washington has been instructed to bring the
                            foregoing to the knowledge of the Government of the United States of
                            America.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
